# Reactive Agents -- Strategy Demo playground
#
# This file is the template. On first boot it is copied to `.env`.
# Open `.env` in the StackBlitz editor, paste your key after the `=`,
# then restart the terminal (the circular-arrow icon).
#
# The demo auto-detects which provider you configured. Any ONE of these
# is enough (free-tier picks: Gemini or Groq):
#
#   Google:    https://ai.google.dev        (GOOGLE_API_KEY, recommended)
#   Anthropic: https://console.anthropic.com (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
#   OpenAI:    https://platform.openai.com   (OPENAI_API_KEY)
#   Groq:      https://console.groq.com      (GROQ_API_KEY, fast + free tier)
#   xAI:       https://console.x.ai          (XAI_API_KEY)
#   LiteLLM:   any OpenAI-compatible proxy   (LITELLM_BASE_URL, 40+ models)

GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://your-proxy:4000

# Optional: force a provider when several keys are present
# PROVIDER=groq

# Optional: choose which strategies to compare (comma-separated).
# Default runs reactive, plan-execute-reflect, and adaptive side-by-side.
# Available: reactive | plan-execute-reflect | tree-of-thought | reflexion |
#            adaptive | blueprint | direct
# STRATEGIES=reactive,tree-of-thought

# Optional: token budget enforced per run (the framework's cost killswitch)
# BUDGET_TOKENS=10000

# Optional: custom task
# TASK=Why is immutability important in functional programming?

# Optional: override the model (blank = provider's current default)
# MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Local Ollama: the WebContainer's "localhost" is NOT your machine, so a
# hosted embed needs an HTTPS tunnel. On your host run:
#   OLLAMA_ORIGINS=* ollama serve
#   cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:11434   (or: ngrok http 11434)
# then uncomment + paste the https URL it prints (Chrome only):
# PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-TUNNEL.trycloudflare.com
# MODEL=llama3.2
